llvm23: LLVM_ABI on AMD's heterogeneous-debug additions (AMD 0bace190 defect)

AMD's heterogeneous-debug additions in 0bace190 (DIExprBuilder, DIOp, new DIExpression
entry points, DIBuilder::createGlobalVariable with a memory space, GlobalVariable debug-info
accessors, Attribute::isSanitizedPaddedGlobal) carry no LLVM_ABI. AMD never builds LLVM as a
Windows DLL (TheRock's Windows LLVM is static libs only), so nothing exports them. Run
38570967283 win-arm64 failed linking clang-cpp.dll on
llvm::DIExprBuilder::DIExprBuilder(LLVMContext&) and DIExprBuilder::intoExpression().
The list comes from a diff of llvm/include against upstream merge-base 3e7a2ec7 and covers
every added non-inline, non-template public declaration with an out-of-line definition in
llvm/lib. Members only, never whole classes (none of these classes is class-annotated).

